/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    The name a Judge arm binds carries no depth, so it reads as made outside every rabbit.

    A call opens no region, so what a function makes lies in whatever region its caller
    has open, and what it hands back is as deep as the call unless all of it comes from
    its parameters. This was accepted, and the compiled program read the value after the
    rabbit's Done. had freed it (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O1). */

Define outer as a series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Define either as a catalogue of (number or series of number) with (0).
    Insert inner into either.
    For each entry in either, repeat:
        Judge entry, where it is:
            A number, state "n".
            A series of number, outer becomes it.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.

/*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State outer.
